    mkg:linkDescription "Bolton 2006 (cake complete blocking) and Bolton 2006 (cake intermediate blocking) are alternative combined fouling models from the same study, evaluated on the same BSA and human plasma IgG filtration systems under constant-pressure and constant-flow operation. Both use Darcy’s law and combine cake growth, which increases flow resistance, with loss of available membrane area; both predict permeate volume or pressure over time and use two fitted parameters. They differ in the blocking mechanism: Bolton 2006 (cake complete blocking) uses complete blocking, while Bolton 2006 (cake intermediate blocking) uses intermediate blocking, in which available area decreases exponentially with processed permeate volume. Bolton 2006 (cake intermediate blocking) fit the constant-flow IgG and constant-pressure BSA data better by reported SSR, while Bolton 2006 (cake complete blocking) fit constant-pressure IgG slightly better." ;
