    mkg:linkDescription "Kontoravdi 2010 and Xing 2010 both model fed-batch mammalian cell cultures producing antibody products, predicting viable-cell concentration, nutrients, metabolites, and product concentration to support process analysis and optimisation. Both represent nutrient-limited growth and effects of extracellular metabolites, including ammonia, and use culture data to calibrate and validate their predictions. Kontoravdi 2010 models HFN7.1 hybridoma cells producing IgG1 and includes intracellular antibody synthesis, assembly, processing, and secretion; Xing 2010 models a CHO cell line producing B1 and uses a lumped, unstructured kinetic description. Kontoravdi 2010 was developed around flask cultures, whereas Xing 2010 was fitted and tested with large-scale bioreactor runs, including 5,000-L and 500-L cultures." ;
