<http://example.org/kg/link/lopezmeza_2016__xing_2010> rdfs:label "López-Meza 2016 ~ Xing 2010" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "López-Meza 2016 and Xing 2010 are unstructured kinetic models of CHO cell cultures producing antibody products, and both describe cell growth and product formation in batch or fed-batch contexts. López-Meza 2016 is a simpler model for recombinant CHO-S cells producing an infliximab biosimilar, relating glucose use to growth and antibody formation to growth rate and viable-cell concentration. Xing 2010 models a proprietary CHO line producing B1 in large-scale fed-batch culture, with coupled balances for nutrients, metabolites, cells, and product, including maintenance and metabolite inhibition. López-Meza 2016 was developed mainly from shake-flask batches and tested in instrumented batch and fed-batch runs; Xing 2010 was calibrated and validated across 5,000-L and 500-L runs using MCMC." ;
