<http://example.org/kg/link/lopezmeza_2016__zentou_2019_monod> rdfs:label "López-Meza 2016 ~ Zentou 2019 (Monod)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "López-Meza 2016 and Zentou 2019 (Monod) are compact, unstructured kinetic models of microbial or cell growth linked to substrate use and product formation, and both include Monod-type growth relationships. López-Meza 2016 models CHO-S cells using glucose and producing an infliximab biosimilar, with a glucose threshold and Luedeking–Piret antibody production; it also tests the product model in fed-batch operation. Zentou 2019 (Monod) models yeast fermentation of molasses to ethanol, linking biomass growth, sugar consumption, and ethanol production through yield coefficients. They are comparable as growth-and-production models, but describe different organisms, products, substrates, and operating modes." ;
