<http://example.org/kg/link/nausch_2023__wang_2019> rdfs:label "Nausch 2023 ~ Wang 2019" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Nausch 2023 and Wang 2019 are mechanistic models of cultured-cell growth in reactors that connect nutrient conditions to biomass formation, so they can be compared as models of nutrient-dependent culture growth. Nausch 2023 models tobacco BY-2 cells, tracking sugar and mineral-nutrient uptake and active and dead biomass; Wang 2019 models D. viridis algae, tracking nitrate and nitrogen quota alongside light-driven carbon allocation to biomass, carbohydrates, and lipids. Nausch 2023 emphasizes Monod-type growth and semi-continuous feeding, while Wang 2019 emphasizes transient light and nitrogen effects on photosynthesis and storage-product formation. They are related by their growth and nutrient-uptake focus, but are not direct alternatives for the same organism or process." ;
    mkg:provenance "written by gpt-6-luna from the two Sups' descriptions and facts, 2026-10-29 (A/B replaced by the model names by code)" ;
