<http://example.org/kg/link/nausch_2023__xing_2010> rdfs:label "Nausch 2023 ~ Xing 2010" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Nausch 2023 and Xing 2010 are lumped kinetic models of cell growth and extracellular nutrient dynamics in stirred-tank bioreactors, and both use Monod-type growth descriptions. They model the same broad phenomena—nutrient uptake and cell growth—in different systems: Nausch 2023 describes tobacco BY-2 plant cells, while Xing 2010 describes CHO cells producing a B1 antibody fusion protein. Nausch 2023 covers batch followed by semi-continuous feeding, sucrose conversion, and separate active and dead biomass; Xing 2010 models daily-fed fed-batch culture with nutrient maintenance, ammonia and lactate inhibition, and product formation. Thus, they are useful to compare as models of bioreactor cell-culture kinetics, but not as competing models of the same culture." ;
    mkg:provenance "written by gpt-6-luna from the two Sups' descriptions and facts, 2026-10-29 (A/B replaced by the model names by code)" ;
