<http://example.org/kg/link/nausch_2023__zentou_2019_andrews> rdfs:label "Nausch 2023 ~ Zentou 2019 (Andrews)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Nausch 2023 and Zentou 2019 (Andrews) are mechanistic stirred-tank culture models that describe biomass growth alongside sugar consumption over time. Nausch 2023 models tobacco BY-2 cells with Monod-type growth and tracks sucrose-derived sugars plus ammonium, nitrate, and phosphate; Zentou 2019 (Andrews) models yeast molasses fermentation with an Andrews law for substrate-inhibited growth and also predicts ethanol. Both include batch cultivation, but Nausch 2023 proceeds to semi-continuous feeding, whereas Zentou 2019 (Andrews) remains batch and shifts from micro-aerobic to anaerobic operation. They are useful to compare as growth-and-substrate models in different biological systems, with different kinetic laws and process outputs." ;
