    mkg:linkDescription "Nausch 2023 and Zentou 2019 (Monod) are unstructured Monod-type models of microbial or plant-cell growth in stirred bioreactors, relating biomass formation to substrate availability. Nausch 2023 models tobacco BY-2 cells in batch followed by semi-continuous operation, tracking active and dead biomass plus multiple nutrients and sugars, including sucrose hydrolysis. Zentou 2019 (Monod) models batch yeast fermentation of molasses with biomass, sugar substrate, and ethanol balances linked by yield coefficients. They therefore share substrate-dependent growth modeling but differ in organisms, process operation, state variables, and complexity; Zentou 2019 (Monod) also omits high-substrate inhibition." ;
