<http://example.org/kg/link/ng_2012__osberghaus_2012_kinetic_sma> rdfs:label "Ng 2012 ~ Osberghaus 2012 (kinetic SMA)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Ng 2012 and Osberghaus 2012 (kinetic SMA) are dynamic mechanistic models of protein chromatography, both representing column transport, dispersion, mass transfer, and protein adsorption. Ng 2012 models human IgG capture on a protein A adsorbent with pH-dependent Langmuir binding and is used to optimize batch productivity under yield, purity, and pressure constraints. Osberghaus 2012 (kinetic SMA) models ion-exchange binding on SP Sepharose FF with steric mass action sorption and focuses on estimating parameters from gradient and breakthrough data to predict chromatograms. Their adsorption models, adsorbents, and process-development goals differ, making their modeling and prediction approaches useful to compare." ;
    mkg:provenance "written by gpt-6-luna from the two Sups' descriptions and facts, 2026-10-29 (A/B replaced by the model names by code)" ;
