<http://example.org/kg/link/osberghaus_2012_kinetic_sma__osberghaus_2012_rapid_equilibrium_sma> rdfs:label "Osberghaus 2012 (kinetic SMA) ~ Osberghaus 2012 (rapid equilibrium SMA)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Osberghaus 2012 (kinetic SMA) and Osberghaus 2012 (rapid equilibrium SMA) describe protein binding and elution in strong cation-exchange chromatography, using the same proteins, SP Sepharose FF column, pH conditions, and comparison of gradient/breakthrough parameter estimation with inverse chromatogram fitting. Both model column transport, particle mass transfer, and steric mass action sorption, and report similar predictive performance and sensitivity to retention-time shifts. Osberghaus 2012 (kinetic SMA) is labeled “Kinetic SMA” and notes kinetic effects omitted from the isothermal fit; Osberghaus 2012 (rapid equilibrium SMA) explicitly describes the formulation as rapid-equilibrium SMA. Thus, they are closely related descriptions of the same study and system, with the distinction focused on the sorption formulation." ;
