<http://example.org/kg/link/seidel_2018_detailed_kinetic_model__seidel_2018_simplified_kinetic_model_dynamic> rdfs:label "Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) ~ Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) and Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) model methanol synthesis from CO, CO₂, and hydrogen over the same Cu/ZnO/Al₂O₃ catalyst, including CO and CO₂ hydrogenation and reverse water-gas shift. Both were fitted to the same 140 steady-state experiments and are intended for changing feed conditions. Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) is a detailed, steady-state algebraic Langmuir–Hinshelwood model based on elementary surface steps; Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) uses lumped kinetics and adds dynamic balances for reactor gas composition and the changing fraction of reduced catalyst centers. Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) also captures feed-switching transients and improves identifiability relative to Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model)." ;
    mkg:provenance "written by gpt-6-luna from the two Sups' descriptions and facts, 2026-10-29 (A/B replaced by the model names by code)" ;
