<http://example.org/kg/link/seidel_2018_detailed_kinetic_model__seidel_2018_simplified_kinetic_model_steady_state> rdfs:label "Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) ~ Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) and Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) model methanol synthesis over Cu/ZnO/Al₂O₃, predicting CO and CO₂ hydrogenation and reverse water-gas shift rates for changing feed compositions. Both were fitted to the same 140 steady-state Micro-Berty experiments and achieved similar fits. Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) uses a detailed Langmuir–Hinshelwood formulation based on elementary surface steps, while Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) uses lumped kinetics and calculates the oxidized/reduced surface-center fractions algebraically from an equilibrium morphology relation. Both steady-state formulations are algebraic; the switching experiments also showed that a dynamic surface-center variant of Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) better captured catalyst lag." ;
