<http://example.org/kg/link/seidel_2018_detailed_kinetic_model__vandenbussche_1996> rdfs:label "Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) ~ Vanden Bussche 1996" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) and Vanden Bussche 1996 are mechanistic steady-state kinetic models of methanol synthesis and the reverse water-gas-shift reaction over commercial Cu/ZnO/Al₂O₃ catalysts, and both address how feed composition and operating conditions affect reaction behavior. They are worth comparing as alternative descriptions of this process; Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model)’s paper specifically compares its predictions with Vanden Bussche 1996. Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) includes explicit CO hydrogenation as well as CO₂ hydrogenation, whereas Vanden Bussche 1996 couples methanol synthesis and reverse water-gas shift through a shared surface oxygen intermediate. Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model) was fitted to differential Micro-Berty reactor experiments using partial pressures, while Vanden Bussche 1996 was fitted to integral bench-reactor conversions and considered fugacities. Seidel 2018 (detailed kinetic model)’s paper reports that Vanden Bussche 1996 could not reproduce its pure-CO experiments and had larger deviations on other experiments." ;
    mkg:provenance "written by gpt-6-luna from the two Sups' descriptions and facts, 2026-10-29 (A/B replaced by the model names by code)" ;
