<http://example.org/kg/link/seidel_2018_simplified_kinetic_model_dynamic__seidel_2018_simplified_kinetic_model_steady_state> rdfs:label "Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) ~ Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) and Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) are variants of the same simplified methanol-synthesis model over a Cu/ZnO/Al₂O₃ catalyst, using lumped Langmuir–Hinshelwood kinetics for CO hydrogenation, CO₂ hydrogenation, and reverse water-gas shift. Both distinguish oxidized and reduced surface centers and were fitted using the same 140 steady-state experiments. Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) calculates the surface-center fraction algebraically from an equilibrium morphology relation, while Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) adds dynamic catalyst-state and reactor balances to represent catalyst lag during feed switches. Thus, Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) extends the quasi-static approach in Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) to capture transients; Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model steady state) focuses on steady-state prediction." ;
