<http://example.org/kg/link/seidel_2018_simplified_kinetic_model_dynamic__vandenbussche_1996> rdfs:label "Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) ~ Vanden Bussche 1996" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) and Vanden Bussche 1996 model methanol synthesis and the reverse water-gas shift over commercial Cu/ZnO/Al₂O₃ catalysts, predicting how reaction conditions affect methanol production and gas composition. Vanden Bussche 1996 is a steady-state mechanistic model with a detailed surface-reaction scheme, fitted using integral bench-reactor experiments; Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) uses simplified, lumped kinetics and adds dynamic catalyst-state and reactor balances to represent feed-switching transients. Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) also includes CO hydrogenation, which the paper says Vanden Bussche 1996 neglects and which prevented Vanden Bussche 1996 from reproducing pure-CO-feed experiments. Their reactor configurations and purposes differ: Vanden Bussche 1996 examines steady-state reactor behavior, while Seidel 2018 (simplified kinetic model dynamic) is aimed at dynamic simulation under changing feeds." ;
