    mkg:linkDescription "Wang 2019 and Xing 2010 are dynamic kinetic models of biological cultivation in bioreactors, each using six coupled equations to predict culture time courses. Wang 2019 models light- and nitrogen-dependent growth and carbon allocation in *Dunaliella viridis* in a flat-panel photobioreactor; Xing 2010 models nutrient-limited growth, metabolite effects, and B1 production in fed-batch CHO cultures. Wang 2019 focuses on photosynthesis, storage compounds, and chlorophyll under changing light and nitrogen, while Xing 2010 focuses on cells, nutrients, metabolites, and antibody-fusion-protein production under daily feeding. Both were calibrated against culture data and tested on separate experiments, but they describe different organisms and cultivation processes." ;
