    mkg:linkDescription "Xing 2010 and Zentou 2019 (Andrews) are dynamic bioreactor-culture models that predict biomass, substrate-related quantities, and product formation, and both represent inhibition affecting cell growth. Xing 2010 models fed-batch CHO production of a B1 fusion protein, with nutrient limitation and inhibition by ammonia and lactate. Zentou 2019 (Andrews) models batch yeast fermentation for ethanol, using the Andrews law to represent inhibition by excess substrate and yield coefficients to link growth, substrate consumption, and ethanol production. They therefore offer comparable growth-and-production modeling approaches, but differ in organism, operating mode, products, and the source of inhibition represented." ;
