    mkg:linkDescription "Zentou 2019 (Andrews) and Zentou 2019 (Monod) are directly compared models of batch molasses fermentation by Saccharomyces cerevisiae, predicting biomass, substrate, and ethanol using growth-linked balances and yield coefficients. They share the same process and purpose, but Zentou 2019 (Andrews) uses an Andrews growth law that represents inhibition at high substrate concentrations, while Zentou 2019 (Monod) uses a Monod law that does not. Zentou 2019 (Andrews)’s parameters were estimated from higher initial substrate concentrations and it performs better at high concentrations; Zentou 2019 (Monod)’s were estimated at low concentrations and it performs better at low concentrations. They are rival formulations intended for use over different operating ranges." ;
